    "updated_at": "2021-07-18T10:13:35Z",
    "body": "That's not entirely satisfactory :)\r\n\r\nTerminal colors are defined in terms of \"<color>\" and \"dark<color>\", like \"cyan\" and \"darkcyan\". Most themes — no matter whether light or dark — seem to reflect the naming in colors, having \"darkgreen\" darker than \"green\". Starship prefers the plain variants, which give a better readability on dark backgrounds. On light backgrounds, dark colors are better.\r\n\r\nWould be nice to have a proper light variant, with terminal colors turned around. This is what Vim's `set background=` does, incidentally.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
