    "created_at": "2023-07-20T17:51:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-07-20T17:51:46Z",
    "body": "This issue is caused by Starship and the terminal emulator disagreeing on what \"intense color\" is supposed to mean.\r\n\r\nKonsole's light color schemes have brighter intense colors than normal colors, and its dark color schemes have darker intense colors than normal ones. So in all cases, Konsole will assign less contrast to intense text. There may be a good reason for Konsole to do this, but it is counterintuitive.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, Starship color palettes presume intense colors to be more contrasting than normal colors. To me this seems natural, but it conflicts with Konsole (and iTerm, as seen in the original report).\r\n\r\nI have not researched other terminal emulators or the historical background around intense colors being less contrasting. Either Starship should refrain from using intense colors everywhere, or we should convince terminal emulators to swap intense and normal colors in their color schemes.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
