    "created_at": "2025-09-29T17:28:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-29T17:28:12Z",
    "body": "> Is there a reasonable workaround until this issue is fixed?\n\nThere absolutely is! If you terminal has decent palettes for both dark and bright theme, you can simply reference the base 16 colors in your format string.\n\n\n```toml\nformat = \"\"\"\n[ $os( $username)](              bg:orange                       )\\\n                            []( bg:yellow       fg:prev_bg      )\\\n                 [ $directory ]( bg:prev_bg      fg:bright-white )\\\n                            []( bg:cyan         fg:prev_bg      )\\\n[( $git_branch( $git_status) )]( bg:prev_bg      fg:bright-white )\\\n$bun$c$cmake$cpp$java$lua$nodejs$python$quarto$rlang\\\n                            []( bg:bright-black fg:prev_bg      )\\\n                [$conda$docker]( bg:prev_bg      fg:bright-white )\\\n                            []( bg:green        fg:prev_bg      )\\\n                    [( $jobs )]( bg:prev_bg      fg:bright-white )\\\n                            [](                 fg:prev_bg      )\\\n$fill\\\n                            [](                 fg:red          )\\\n                  [( $status )]( bg:red          fg:bright-white )\\\n                            []( bg:red          fg:purple       )\\\n            [( $cmd_duration )]( bg:purple       fg:bright-white )\\\n                            []( bg:prev_bg      fg:black        )\\\n                      [ $time ]( bg:black        fg:bright-white )\\\n$line_break $shell\n\"\"\"\n```\n\nHere, except `orange`, all colors are defined in terminal instead of palette.\n\nHowever this solution is not perfect, as some of the text (fg colors) still lack contrast.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
